# DriveMind AI — Project Rules

`AGENTS.md` is the source of truth for project instructions. Read it first. This file only keeps the short summary below in line with it; if they disagree, `AGENTS.md` and the code win.

## What This Project Is

A Google Drive knowledge assistant: it syncs read-only Drive content, builds a hybrid (vector + keyword + metadata) index, and answers questions with source citations. Not a simple PDF chatbot, not a ChatGPT clone, not a file manager.

- Stack: Next.js 15 / React 19 / TypeScript, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy/asyncpg, PostgreSQL, Qdrant, OpenAI, LangGraph, Tesseract OCR.
- Drive access is read-only. The model never reads Drive; it receives retrieved chunks only.
- Chunk text is authoritative in PostgreSQL; embeddings live in Qdrant under the same chunk UUID.
- Answer paths (all must keep working): the linear hybrid path (default), the optional LangGraph path (`AGENT_GRAPH_ENABLED`), and the tool-calling agent (`TOOL_RAG_AGENT_ENABLED`, default false), which is the path the evaluation harness measures.
- Authentication and ownership are in a mixed state: chat, files, sources and conversations use application sessions; sync, ingestion and chunking still fall back to the first stored OAuth token. Do not assume full multi-user isolation. Details: `AGENTS.md`, "Known Important Constraints".

## Where Things Are

- `backend/app/`: `api/` routes only, `services/` business logic, `retrieval/`, `ingestion/`, `agents/` (`tool_rag/`, `drive_graph/`), `connectors/google_drive/`, `llm/`, `embeddings/`, `db/`, `core/` config.
- `frontend/`: Next.js, calls only the FastAPI REST API (`/api/v1`).
- Supported file types: Google Docs, Sheets and Slides, TXT, Markdown, CSV, PDF (text only, no scanned-PDF OCR), DOCX, PPTX, XLSX, images (Tesseract). See `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Rules

- Coding and review rules: `CODING_STANDARDS.md`. Commands and constraints: `AGENTS.md`.
- Keep changes scoped. Add or update tests with every behavior change. Preserve the public API, citation contracts and status semantics.
- Never commit `.env`, tokens, credentials, Drive downloads or database volumes.
- Do not commit, push or deploy unless the owner explicitly asks.

